BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Evening Book Club & Play Reading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:6972a805d2bbe265eb294671@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join other book lovers in your community and participate in li
 vely discussions of popular books.\nMeeting every 1\nst\nTuesday of the mo
 nth. We will be discussing the following:\nFebruary 3\, 2026\n– The No-S
 how by Beth O-Leary\nMarch 3\, 2026\n– Hello Beautiful by Ann Napolitano
 \nApril 7\, 2026\n– The Housekeeper by Joy Fielding\nMay 5\, 2026\n– T
 he Dutch Orphan by Ellen Keith\nCopies of the book are available for borro
 wing at the Fairview Library.\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration 
 necessary.
LOCATION:Fairview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6972a805d2bbe265eb294671
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Financial Workshops for Seniors with John Stapleton: Protecting Yo
 ur Retirement Income
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T160000
UID:69b1ef72491b809c6f1fc096@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join social policy expert John Stapleton to plan for your fina
 ncial future.\nIf you are a low-income earner or advise low-income earners
 \, this program will help you understand:\nProtecting Your Retirement Inco
 me\nLearn how you can reduce clawbacks to your GIS and GAINS payments if y
 ou have additional income from employment\, a private pension\, or a Regis
 tered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP).\nThis is a drop-in program. Registra
 tion is not required.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1ef72491b809c6f1fc096
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
