BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 4: Formatting Reports and Long Documents
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260422T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260422T153000
UID:699f5fab4dacf581ff7de7ec@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Practice your Microsoft Word skills when working with long doc
 uments.\nIn this class\, you will:\nUse Styles to effectively format\, str
 ucture and navigate your document\nCreate a Table of Contents\nUse Page an
 d Section breaks\nInsert Page Numbers and Footnotes\nInsert Web and docume
 nt links\nLearn about Microsoft Word's Accessibility features\nUpon comple
 tion of this class\, you will be able to format long documents\, such as b
 ooks\, reports\, and essays.\nPrerequisites:  Word Basics 1\, 2 & 3\, or e
 quivalent skills. Keyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nFormat: Hand
 s-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Northern District\, eLearning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f5fab4dacf581ff7de7ec
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 1: Write a Letter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T143000
UID:69ab681d8089f23c676059bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Word for absolute beginners
 .\nIn this class\, you will:\nUnderstand how to use Word’s Tabs\, Groups
 \, and Commands\nCreate\, save\, print and delete Word documents\nPractice
  basic text formatting and style features\nUpon completion of this class\,
  you will be able to use Microsoft Word at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: 
 Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demons
 trations\nDrop In.
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab681d8089f23c676059bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
