BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transforming Garbage: Collage a Postcard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T150000
UID:69a206a68d5e2d09336219cd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Gain an understanding of creating art with upcycled materials
  through the art of collage. By using magazines and a card stock surface
 \, participants will start cutting out images and words that relate to the
 ir desired work of art. This workshop will encourage the process of workin
 g with collage as a non-precious material and inspire participants to cr
 eate a piece of art with the materials in their own home/community.\nThis 
 workshop will be delivered by Alysha Rocca\, an emerging artist who holds
  a BFA from OCAD University. Working with the theme of sustainability\, A
 lysha weaves together the threads of feminism and environmental conscious
 ness.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square - Closed\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a206a68d5e2d09336219cd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T143000
UID:69e1172c8ddc1caf5f1d58f9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Room B
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e1172c8ddc1caf5f1d58f9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
